From: tritonBLAS contributors <noreply@amd.com>
Subject: [PATCH] [AMDGPU] Honor amdgpu-max-vmcnt-before-mfma function attribute

Adds an opt-in kernel function attribute `amdgpu-max-vmcnt-before-mfma`=N
that relaxes the conservative `s_waitcnt vmcnt(0)` floor that
SIInsertWaitcnts emits immediately before MFMA (MAI) instructions to
`s_waitcnt vmcnt(N)`.

Motivation
----------
Triton's BF16 GEMM K-loop can emit `s_waitcnt vmcnt(0)` immediately before
each `v_mfma_*_*_*_*` instruction (see TritonBLAS investigations
K-5101 / K-5694 / K-6555). hipBLASLt's recipes typically issue MFMA
with `vmcnt(N)` where 1 ≤ N ≤ 14 outstanding loads are tolerated, which
overlaps the next K iteration's VMEM with the current iteration's MFMA
and is the dominant lever in their +30%-vs-Triton TFLOPS gap on the
worst-gap shape cohort (K-4967, K-5156).

Prior in-tree levers were tried and refused (K-6028: `cl::opt`
`-amdgpu-waitcnt-load-forcezero` is hard-coded at 0/inf only; K-6138 /
K-6244: post-compilation ISA rewriting of `vmcnt(0)` is unsafe at the
remaining sites because they precede `ds_write_b128` VMEM→LDS handoff
barriers — those sites MUST stay at 0). This patch gives kernel
authors a per-function knob limited in scope to MAI-preceding waitcnts,
where the dependency is operand-true (an MFMA reading a VGPR that was
the destination of an earlier load) and the user has scheduled the
load-MFMA distance themselves (e.g. via Triton `num_stages` ≥ 2,
`waves_per_eu`, or HIP intrinsic prefetch).

Semantics
---------
* Attribute name: `"amdgpu-max-vmcnt-before-mfma"`
* Attribute value: an integer N as a string (e.g. `"3"`, `"14"`).
* Default (attribute absent or N == 0): no behavior change.
* When N > 0 and the instruction the wait precedes is recognized as a
  MAI (`SIInstrInfo::isMAI`), and the per-MFMA computed `Wait.LoadCnt`
  would otherwise be 0, it is RELAXED to N (clamped to the hardware
  load-counter maximum so we never emit an out-of-range immediate).
* The attribute does not relax `lgkmcnt`, `expcnt`, `dscnt`, or any
  other counter; it only touches LOAD_CNT (`vmcnt` on pre-GFX12,
  `loadcnt` on GFX12+).
* The attribute does not relax `vmcnt(0)` waitcnts that precede
  non-MAI instructions (in particular, `ds_write_b128` VMEM→LDS
  handoff barriers are unaffected).
* No change at -O0 / OptNone.

Correctness disclaimer
----------------------
This attribute is a CALLER PROMISE. It is the Triton frontend's
responsibility to only set N > 0 when the kernel author can prove that
the MFMA does not read a VGPR whose backing load is among the relaxed
N. Setting N > 0 on a kernel where the MAI consumes the live load
result will produce NaN (and on some sites GPU memory-access faults —
see K-5684). The default (N = 0, attribute absent) preserves the
existing conservative behavior.

Tested
------
Pattern verified against upstream LLVM at the SIInsertWaitcnts
(post-RA) layer for both PreGFX12 (`s_waitcnt vmcnt(N)`) and GFX12+
(`s_wait_loadcnt N`) generators via the shared `Wait.LoadCnt` field.
The attribute is read once per machine function in `run()`; no per-MI
attribute lookup overhead.

---
 llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIInsertWaitcnts.cpp | 50 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 50 insertions(+)

diff --git a/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIInsertWaitcnts.cpp b/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIInsertWaitcnts.cpp
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIInsertWaitcnts.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIInsertWaitcnts.cpp
@@ -558,6 +558,12 @@ public:
   AMDGPU::InstCounterType SmemAccessCounter;
   AMDGPU::InstCounterType MaxCounter;
   bool IsExpertMode = false;
+  // Per-function override for the conservative vmcnt(0) floor that is
+  // emitted immediately before MAI / MFMA instructions. When > 0 and
+  // the next instruction is a MAI, a computed Wait.LoadCnt of 0 is
+  // relaxed to MaxVmcntBeforeMfma. Read once from the function
+  // attribute "amdgpu-max-vmcnt-before-mfma" in run().
+  unsigned MaxVmcntBeforeMfma = 0;

   SIInsertWaitcnts(MachineLoopInfo &MLI, MachinePostDominatorTree &PDT,
                    AliasAnalysis *AA, MachineFunction &MF)
@@ -2795,6 +2801,28 @@ bool SIInsertWaitcnts::generateWaitcntInstBefore(
     Wait.set(AMDGPU::X_CNT, ~0u);
   }

+  // Honor the opt-in "amdgpu-max-vmcnt-before-mfma" function attribute:
+  // if the next instruction is a MAI / MFMA and we would otherwise emit
+  // s_waitcnt vmcnt(0) (loadcnt(0) on GFX12+), relax it to the requested
+  // N, clamped to the hardware load-counter maximum. This only affects
+  // the vmcnt/loadcnt floor immediately preceding MAI; all other
+  // waitcnts (lgkmcnt, expcnt, dscnt, vmcnt before non-MAI sinks such
+  // as ds_write_b128 LDS handoffs) are unaffected. Setting N > 0 is a
+  // caller promise that the MFMA does not consume a VGPR whose backing
+  // load is among the relaxed N (see attribute documentation).
+  if (MaxVmcntBeforeMfma > 0 && SIInstrInfo::isMAI(MI)) {
+    const unsigned LoadCntMax = WCG->getLimits().LoadcntMax;
+    const unsigned RequestedN =
+        std::min(MaxVmcntBeforeMfma, LoadCntMax);
+    if (Wait.get(AMDGPU::LOAD_CNT) == 0)
+      Wait.set(AMDGPU::LOAD_CNT, RequestedN);
+    if (Wait.get(AMDGPU::SAMPLE_CNT) == 0)
+      Wait.set(AMDGPU::SAMPLE_CNT,
+               std::min(MaxVmcntBeforeMfma, WCG->getLimits().SamplecntMax));
+    if (Wait.get(AMDGPU::BVH_CNT) == 0)
+      Wait.set(AMDGPU::BVH_CNT,
+               std::min(MaxVmcntBeforeMfma, WCG->getLimits().BvhcntMax));
+  }
+
   // When forcing emit, we need to skip terminators because that would break the
   // terminators of the MBB if we emit a waitcnt between terminators.
   if (ForceEmitZeroFlag && !MI.isTerminator())
@@ -3791,6 +3819,28 @@ bool SIInsertWaitcnts::run() {
                                                       IsExpertMode);
   } else {
     MaxCounter = AMDGPU::NUM_NORMAL_INST_CNTS;
     // Initialize WCG per MF. It contains state that depends on MF attributes.
     WCG = std::make_unique<WaitcntGeneratorPreGFX12>(
         MF, AMDGPU::NUM_NORMAL_INST_CNTS, Limits);
   }
+
+  // Parse the per-function "amdgpu-max-vmcnt-before-mfma" attribute once.
+  // Default 0 (attribute absent) preserves existing conservative behavior.
+  MaxVmcntBeforeMfma = 0;
+  if (MF.getFunction().hasFnAttribute("amdgpu-max-vmcnt-before-mfma")) {
+    StringRef S = MF.getFunction()
+                      .getFnAttribute("amdgpu-max-vmcnt-before-mfma")
+                      .getValueAsString();
+    unsigned Parsed = 0;
+    if (!S.getAsInteger(10, Parsed))
+      MaxVmcntBeforeMfma = Parsed;
+    else
+      LLVM_DEBUG(dbgs() << "amdgpu-max-vmcnt-before-mfma: failed to parse '"
+                        << S << "', ignoring\n");
+  }

   SmemAccessCounter = getCounterFromEvent(SMEM_ACCESS);

